<p class="legal__updated">Last updated: 5 October 2026</p>

<h2>1. Data controller</h2>
<p>The controller of your personal data is Festilaw B.V., a private limited company incorporated under Dutch law, with its registered office in Nijmegen, Spoorstraat 30A, 6511 AN Nijmegen, the Netherlands, registered with the Netherlands Chamber of Commerce (KvK) under number 77058720.</p>
<p>For any question regarding your personal data: <a href="mailto:team@festilaw.com">team@festilaw.com</a></p>
<p>Festilaw B.V. has not appointed a Data Protection Officer, as this is not mandatory in view of its activities.</p>

<h2>2. Data processed, purposes and legal bases</h2>
<p><strong>Contact requests.</strong> When you contact us through the contact form or by email, we process your name, email address, website or shop URL and the content of your message in order to respond to your request and, where appropriate, to send you a commercial proposal. This processing is based on steps taken at your request prior to entering into a contract (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR) or, where your request does not relate to our services, on our legitimate interest in responding to messages sent to us (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).</p>
<p><strong>Client relationship.</strong> When your company becomes a client, we process the business contact details of the contact persons designated by the client, our correspondence, and the documents provided in the course of our services (responsible economic operator mandate, documentary audit). This processing is necessary for the performance of the contract concluded with your company (Article 6(1)(b)) and for our legitimate interest in managing the business relationship with its representatives (Article 6(1)(f)).</p>
<p><strong>Client area and electronic signature.</strong> Our clients can access, through a secure client area, the documents they have sent us. For this purpose, clients access their file through a secure personal link sent by email, without an account or password; we process the contact person's name and email address, connection data and the documents made available in the client area. Contracts and certain documents are signed electronically; the electronic signature service records the signatories' names, email addresses, IP addresses and the time-stamped audit trail of the signature. This processing is necessary for the performance of the contract concluded with your company (Article 6(1)(b)) and for our legitimate interest in providing our clients' representatives with secure access to their documents (Article 6(1)(f)).</p>
<p><strong>Regulatory obligations.</strong> As the responsible economic operator within the meaning of Article 16 of Regulation (EU) 2023/988 and Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, Festilaw B.V. is required to retain certain documents and to cooperate with market surveillance authorities. Personal data contained in these documents are processed on the basis of these legal obligations (Article 6(1)(c)). The same applies to Dutch accounting and tax obligations.</p>
<p><strong>Website operation and security.</strong> Our hosting provider records technical connection data (IP address, date and time, pages visited, browser type) necessary for the operation and security of the website. This processing is based on our legitimate interest in ensuring the availability and security of the website (Article 6(1)(f)).</p>
<p>We do not carry out any automated decision-making or profiling.</p>

<h2>3. Recipients</h2>
<p>Your data are accessible only to Festilaw B.V. and, to the extent necessary, to the following recipients:</p>
<ul>
    <li>our hosting provider, Hostinger International Ltd. (Cyprus), which hosts the website and the client area;</li>
    <li>our electronic signature provider, Docsketch, LLC (trading as SignWell), established in the United States;</li>
    <li>our payment service provider, Stripe Payments Europe, Limited (Ireland);</li>
    <li>Google Ireland Limited (Google Calendar), for booking consultations;</li>
    <li>our email service provider, Plus Five Five, Inc. (trading as Resend), established in the United States;</li>
    <li>our accountant, for data required for invoicing;</li>
    <li>market surveillance authorities and other competent public authorities, where we are required by law to provide them with information.</li>
</ul>
<p>Our service providers act as processors, on our instructions and under a contract compliant with Article 28 GDPR. We do not sell or rent your data.</p>

<h2>4. Transfers outside the European Union</h2>
<p>Our electronic signature provider, SignWell, and our email service provider, Resend, are established in the United States; our payment service provider, Stripe, and Google, for booking consultations, may transfer personal data to their parent companies in the United States (Stripe, Inc. and Google LLC). These transfers are carried out on the basis of the Standard Contractual Clauses adopted by the European Commission (Article 46(2)(c) GDPR). You may obtain a copy of these safeguards by writing to <a href="mailto:team@festilaw.com">team@festilaw.com</a>.</p>
<p>In addition, as our clients are established outside the European Union, our exchanges with them may involve the communication of personal data to the country in which they are established. Such transfers take place either to a country covered by an adequacy decision of the European Commission, or because they are necessary for the performance of the contract concluded with the client (Article 49(1)(b) GDPR).</p>

<h2>5. Retention periods</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Contact requests not followed up: twelve months from the last exchange.</li>
    <li>Client data: for the duration of the contractual relationship, then seven years for accounting and tax records, in accordance with Dutch tax law.</li>
    <li>Access to the client area: for the duration of the contractual relationship; personal access links are deactivated when the relationship ends.</li>
    <li>Documents retained in our capacity as responsible economic operator: for the entire duration of the mandate. Upon its termination, the documents are returned to the client or transferred to the new responsible economic operator it designates, and our copies are destroyed, except for those we are required to retain under the legislation applicable to the products concerned, as a rule for up to ten years after the last product covered by the mandate was placed on the market.</li>
    <li>Signed contracts and their signature audit trail: for the duration of the contractual relationship, then for the applicable limitation period.</li>
    <li>Connection data: for a limited period determined by our hosting provider, and no longer than necessary to ensure the security of the website.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Your rights</h2>
<p>You have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing and data portability, as well as the right to object to processing based on our legitimate interest. These rights are exercised within the limits set by the GDPR; in particular, we cannot erase data that we are required by law to retain.</p>
<p>To exercise your rights, please write to <a href="mailto:team@festilaw.com">team@festilaw.com</a>. We will respond within one month, which may be extended by two months for complex requests. We may ask you to verify your identity where there is reasonable doubt.</p>
<p>You may lodge a complaint with the Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens (<a href="https://www.autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl" rel="noopener">www.autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl</a>) or with the supervisory authority of the Member State of your habitual residence, place of work or place of the alleged infringement.</p>

<h2>7. Security</h2>
<p>Festilaw B.V. implements appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your data against loss, unauthorised access or disclosure, including encryption of connections to the website (HTTPS), access to the client area through unique, secure personal links, and restricting access to those who need it.</p>

<h2>8. Cookies</h2>
<p>This website only uses cookies that are strictly necessary for its operation, including a session cookie required for the website and the client area to function, which do not require consent.</p>

<h2>9. Changes</h2>
<p>We may amend this policy to reflect changes in our processing activities or in the applicable regulations. The date of the latest update is shown at the top of this document.</p>
